cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OdontoAge in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "OdontoAge: an open reference implementation of dental age-estimation methods"
abstract: >-
  OdontoAge is an open-source, cross-verified, tested reference implementation of the
  classic dental age-estimation methods (Cameriere open-apex and pulp/tooth-area formulas,
  Demirjian maturity scoring, Willems direct-age tables, and Kvaal adult pulp/tooth ratios).
  It provides a Python library, a command-line tool, and a zero-install web application,
  each producing an estimated age with a confidence interval, a transparent reasoning
  trace, and the source citation. It is intended for research and education only.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Boustani Hezarani"
    given-names: "Hossein"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-8481-0498"
